  "confidence": "medium",
  "defer": false,
  "narrative": "Belmont Stores is leaking value through order behaviour, not headline revenue: purchases are splitting into many smaller orders rather than shrinking outright. Order frequency jumped 73.9% while basket width and order value each fell 42-47%, far outside normal variation. This shift held across the last two quarters, suggesting a structural change such as multi-sourcing rather than a seasonal blip.",
  "attributed_categories": [],
  "cited_evidence": [
    "Order frequency rose from 2.11 to 3.67 orders per month, a 73.9% increase since baseline.",
    "Average basket width fell from 3.79 to 2.18 product lines per order, down 42.5%.",
    "Average order value dropped from \u20b998,111 to \u20b951,737 per order, down 47.3%.",
    "Overall revenue drifted down only 8.4%, from \u20b9207,007 to \u20b9189,704 a month, within this account's normal swing.",
    "Product losses were spread across five categories, including Power Tools and Diagnostic Equipment, with none dominating and none stopped entirely."
  ],
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Contact Belmont Stores to check if purchasing is being split across multiple suppliers.",
    "Review the recent account manager handover for gaps in order coordination.",
    "Track basket width and order frequency next quarter to confirm the pattern persists."
  ],
